    "uid": "60d78f8ee91fc1271701f9673a5dd63c",
    "title": "Netcat or socat invoked",
    "desc": "netcat (nc, ncat, netcat) or socat ran. These move bytes over a raw socket - a bind or reverse shell, an ad-hoc file transfer, a port probe, a quick relay - so on a host where they are not part of the toolkit any run is worth a look (MITRE T1095). They are also an everyday admin convenience on plenty of boxes, which is exactly why this ships optional: switch it on where netcat has no business running, leave it off where it is normal. reverse_shell and tunnel_tool catch the specific malicious shapes host-wide; this is the blanket policy alert on the tool itself.",
